function.arguments:
{
  "description": "Formulate a MILP for integrated train rescheduling and speed management under partial segment blockage. Variables: binary route choice r_{t,s} (train t uses side s of segment), binary order o_{i,j} (train i precedes j on shared track), continuous arrival a_{t,n}, departure d_{t,n} at station n, travel time τ_{t,seg} on segment, speed level v_{t,seg} (discretized). Objective: minimize weighted sum of total delay Σ_t (a_{t,last}-scheduled_arrival_t) and energy consumption Σ_t Σ_seg e(v_{t,seg})·τ_{t,seg}. Constraints: (1) each train chooses exactly one side on blocked segment; (2) if both trains on same side, enforce ordering: a_j >= d_i + safety_gap * o_{i,j}; (3) if opposite sides, no conflict. (4) time feasibility: d_{t,n}=a_{t,n}+dwell_n. (5) travel time linked to speed: τ_{t,seg}=length_seg / v_{t,seg}. (6) speed limits: v_min ≤ v_{t,seg} ≤ v_max. (7) binary ordering consistency: o_{i,j}+o_{j,i}=1 for any pair sharing track. (8) disruption window: trains cannot occupy blocked side during [T_start,T_end]. (9) optional cancellation binary c_t with big-M on times. Provide all sets, parameters, and big-M values. Assume discretized speed levels L. Provide linearization for product o_{i,j}*τ etc using big-M. Return full model."
}

